    "body": "> Should the declarative shadow tree PR be made ready for merge first? Currently this PR suggests some shared code paths that are meant to not be shared. I.e., `DOMParser` and `parseUnsafeHTML` will deal with declarative shadow trees differently.\r\n\r\nThe plan was to land this one first and then modify the DSD PR accordingly. In that PR, all of the `DOMParser` changes can be reverted, for example. I think the only linkage that will be left will be the flag controlling whether DSD content can be parsed, which will be default-\"no\" but set to \"yes\" by `parseHTMLUnsafe()`. Would that work?",
